<!DOCTYPE node PUBLIC
"-//freedesktop//DTD D-BUS Object Introspection 1.0//EN"
"http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/introspect.dtd">
<node>

  <!--
      io.furios.Shell:
      @short_description: FuriOS additions to the shell

      Shell requests that are specific to FuriOS and so have no home on an
      upstream interface. One interface for all of them, so that later
      additions need no new interface and no new export.

      A separate interface rather than extra methods on the GNOME ones:
      those are defined upstream and are not ours to add to.
  -->
  <interface name="io.furios.Shell">

    <!--
        ScreenshotDelayed:
        @delay: How many seconds to wait before shooting

        Fold the settings drawer away and take a screenshot @delay seconds
        later.

        This exists for the screenshot quick setting, which lives inside the
        very drawer that has to close for the shot to be worth taking: taken
        immediately it would only ever be a picture of the drawer. The wait
        also buys time to bring up whatever was meant to be captured, and is
        counted down in a transient notification.

        The timer belongs to the shell rather than to the caller, because a
        quick setting is destroyed with the drawer it sits in and a timer
        owned by a widget that is going away may never fire.

        Returns as soon as the countdown has started, not when the
        screenshot has been written.
    -->
    <method name="ScreenshotDelayed">
      <arg type="u" direction="in" name="delay"/>
    </method>

  </interface>
</node>
